{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.111:0.2", "PA_thag_1.111:0.3"], "en": "Dvādasamavagga (The Twelfth Chapter)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.111:0.4"], "en": "The Verses of the Elder Jenta:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.111:1.1"], "en": "“Indeed, it is difficult to go forth from home, and difficult to dwell there;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.111:1.2"], "en": "the Dhamma is profound, and wealth is difficult to acquire.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.111:1.3"], "en": "\"Difficult is our livelihood by means of this or that;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.111:1.4"], "en": "it is fitting to constantly contemplate impermanence. ...", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thag_1.111:1.5"], "en": "[Spoken by] the Elder Jenta.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:24:12Z"}
